   "id": "adx_trend",
   "name": "ADX trend (Wilder)",
   "family": "Trend",
   "added_at": "2026-11-08",
   "idea": "Welles Wilder's Directional Movement Index (1978): ADX measures how strong a trend is and +DI / -DI which side is pushing. The classic rule enters only when the trend is strong and pointing up.",
   "why": "A published trend-strength rule with settings fixed by its author (14 bars, 25 level). Unlike the moving-average and breakout rules in the library it trades only when the trend is strong, so it tests whether filtering by trend strength helps.",
